IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `spr-dates`
IMPORT `spr-nouns`
IMPORT `spr-part1-general`
IMPORT `spr-part3-deferral`

-- State Pension Regulations 2015 (S.I. 2015/173), revised text at 2026-04-06.
--
-- LAYER 1, PART 6: regulations 15 to 20 (graduated retirement benefit: what a surviving
-- spouse or civil partner inherits).
-- Written from the text alone and from no one's point of view.
--
-- Graduated retirement benefit (GRB) was an earnings-related addition to the old
-- state pension, paid on graduated contributions between 1961 and 1975 (regulation
-- 1(4) says only: any benefit under sections 36 or 37 of the 1965 Act).
-- Not among the inputs, so taken as plain inputs below:
--   * the deceased's weekly GRB (the 1965 Act and the up-rating orders under section 150
--     of the Administration Act that regulations 16(5) and 20(4) ask for);
--   * the dates on which a person reaches pensionable age (the Pensions Act 1995);
--   * the lump sum of regulation 19 (Schedule 1 to the Social Security (Graduated
--     Retirement Benefit) Regulations 2005);
--   * "section 8(2) choice" (the 2014 Act).
-- Regulation 1(3) means these Regulations do not apply to a person who reaches
-- pensionable age before 6 April 2016 (fork F8); this module does not gate on it,
-- because the seat does (see spr-part1-general.l4).

§ `Part 6: Graduated Retirement Benefit`

§§ `Shared facts: the death of a spouse or civil partner`

DECLARE SpouseDeathFacts HAS
    `the day on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
    `the date the person reaches pensionable age` IS A DATE
    `the kind of relationship` IS A KindOfRelationship
    `the spouse or civil partner died while the two were married or civil partners of each other` IS A BOOLEAN
    `either of them was married to a third person at the time of the death` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date the spouse or civil partner died` IS A DATE
    `the person has married or formed a civil partnership between the date of death and the date they reached pensionable age` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE AgeAtDeath IS ONE OF
    `under pensionable age`
    `over pensionable age`
    `exactly at pensionable age, which is neither under nor over it`

-- "Under" and "over" pensionable age are read as strictly before and strictly after the
-- date the person reaches it; on that date itself the person is neither (fork F20).
GIVEN facts IS A SpouseDeathFacts
GIVETH A AgeAtDeath
`the person's age when the spouse or civil partner died` facts MEANS
    IF facts's `the date the spouse or civil partner died` LESS THAN facts's `the date the person reaches pensionable age`
    THEN `under pensionable age`
    ELSE IF facts's `the date the spouse or civil partner died` GREATER THAN facts's `the date the person reaches pensionable age`
         THEN `over pensionable age`
         ELSE `exactly at pensionable age, which is neither under nor over it`

GIVEN facts IS A SpouseDeathFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person has reached pensionable age on the day` facts MEANS
    facts's `the date the person reaches pensionable age` AT MOST facts's `the day on which the question is asked`

-- The spouse "died while they were married" or the civil partner "while they were civil
-- partners of each other", with regulation 1(5) applied.
GIVEN facts IS A SpouseDeathFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the spouse or civil partner died while the two were married or civil partners` facts MEANS
        facts's `the spouse or civil partner died while the two were married or civil partners of each other`
    AND `regulation 1(5): the two people are treated as spouses or civil partners at the time` (facts's `the kind of relationship`) (facts's `either of them was married to a third person at the time of the death`)

§§ `Regulation 16: the inherited amount`

DECLARE InheritedAmountFacts HAS
    `the date the spouse or civil partner reached pensionable age` IS A DATE
    `the weekly rate of the deceased's graduated retirement benefit, determined in accordance with regulation 16(5)` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE InheritedAmountCase IS ONE OF
    `regulation 16(1) applies`
    `regulation 16(2) applies`
    `regulation 16(3) applies`

-- Gloss, paragraph (1): the spouse died before 6 April 2016, the person was under
-- pensionable age then, and has not married again before reaching it.
-- src:158 | (1) For the purposes of regulation 15(2)(d), a person is entitled to an inherited amount if—
-- src:159 | (a) their spouse or civil partner died before 6th April 2016;
-- src:160 | (b) they were under pensionable age when their spouse or civil partner died; and
-- src:161 | (c) they have not married or formed a civil partnership after the death and before the time they reach pensionable age.
@ref Regulation 16(1) (src:158-161)
GIVEN facts IS A SpouseDeathFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 16(1): the person is entitled to an inherited amount` facts MEANS
        facts's `the date the spouse or civil partner died` LESS THAN `regulation 1(2): the commencement date`
    AND `the person's age when the spouse or civil partner died` facts EQUALS `under pensionable age`
    AND NOT (facts's `the person has married or formed a civil partnership between the date of death and the date they reached pensionable age`)

-- Gloss, paragraph (2): the spouse had reached pensionable age before 6 April 2016 but
-- died on or after it; the person was under pensionable age then, and has not married
-- again before reaching it.
-- src:162 | (2) For the purposes of regulation 15(2)(d), a person is entitled to an inherited amount if—
-- src:163 | (a) their spouse or civil partner reached pensionable age before 6th April 2016 but died on or after 6th April 2016;
-- src:164 | (b) they were under pensionable age when their spouse or civil partner died; and
-- src:165 | (c) they have not married or formed a civil partnership after the death and before the time they reach pensionable age.
@ref Regulation 16(2) (src:162-165)
GIVEN facts IS A SpouseDeathFacts
      spouse IS A InheritedAmountFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 16(2): the person is entitled to an inherited amount` facts spouse MEANS
        spouse's `the date the spouse or civil partner reached pensionable age` LESS THAN `regulation 1(2): the commencement date`
    AND facts's `the date the spouse or civil partner died` AT LEAST `regulation 1(2): the commencement date`
    AND `the person's age when the spouse or civil partner died` facts EQUALS `under pensionable age`
    AND NOT (facts's `the person has married or formed a civil partnership between the date of death and the date they reached pensionable age`)

-- Gloss, paragraph (3): as paragraph (2)(a), but the person was OVER pensionable age
-- when the spouse died.
-- src:166 | (3) For the purposes of regulation 15(2)(d), a person is entitled to an inherited amount if—
-- src:167 | (a) their spouse or civil partner reached pensionable age before 6th April 2016 but died on or after 6th April 2016; and
-- src:168 | (b) they were over pensionable age when their spouse or civil partner died.
@ref Regulation 16(3) (src:166-168)
GIVEN facts IS A SpouseDeathFacts
      spouse IS A InheritedAmountFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 16(3): the person is entitled to an inherited amount` facts spouse MEANS
        spouse's `the date the spouse or civil partner reached pensionable age` LESS THAN `regulation 1(2): the commencement date`
    AND facts's `the date the spouse or civil partner died` AT LEAST `regulation 1(2): the commencement date`
    AND `the person's age when the spouse or civil partner died` facts EQUALS `over pensionable age`

GIVEN facts IS A SpouseDeathFacts
      spouse IS A InheritedAmountFacts
GIVETH A MAYBE InheritedAmountCase
`regulation 16: which paragraph gives the person an inherited amount` facts spouse MEANS
    IF `regulation 16(1): the person is entitled to an inherited amount` facts
    THEN JUST `regulation 16(1) applies`
    ELSE IF `regulation 16(2): the person is entitled to an inherited amount` facts spouse
         THEN JUST `regulation 16(2) applies`
         ELSE IF `regulation 16(3): the person is entitled to an inherited amount` facts spouse
              THEN JUST `regulation 16(3) applies`
              ELSE NOTHING

-- Gloss, paragraph (6): the date on which the deceased's GRB rate is worked out is the
-- date the person reaches pensionable age (cases (1) and (2)), or the date the spouse or
-- civil partner died (case (3)).
-- src:179 | (6) The date mentioned in paragraph (4) is—
-- src:180 | (a) where the person falls within paragraph (1) or (2), the date on which the person reaches pensionable age; or
-- src:181 | (b) where the person falls within paragraph (3), the date on which the person’s spouse or civil partner died.
@ref Regulation 16(6) (src:179-181)
GIVEN facts IS A SpouseDeathFacts
      inheritedCase IS A InheritedAmountCase
GIVETH A DATE
`regulation 16(6): the date as at which the deceased's graduated retirement benefit rate is determined` facts inheritedCase MEANS
    CONSIDER inheritedCase
    WHEN `regulation 16(1) applies` THEN facts's `the date the person reaches pensionable age`
    WHEN `regulation 16(2) applies` THEN facts's `the date the person reaches pensionable age`
    WHEN `regulation 16(3) applies` THEN facts's `the date the spouse or civil partner died`

-- Paragraph (5) says how the weekly rate is determined: the rate for the graduated
-- contributions the deceased paid, as if the section 150 up-rating orders in force since
-- the death had been in force before it, leaving out additions under section 36(4) or
-- 37(1) of the 1965 Act. The orders and the 1965 Act are not inputs, so the result of
-- that determination is the input to paragraph (4).
-- src:169 | (4) The inherited amount is half of the weekly rate of the deceased spouse’s or civil partner’s graduated retirement benefit, determined in accordance with paragraph (5), on the date referred to in paragraph (6) (whether or not the deceased was receiving, or entitled to receive, any such benefit).
-- src:170 | (5) The determination for the purposes of paragraph (4) is carried out by—
-- src:171 | (a) taking the weekly rate of graduated retirement benefit appropriate to the amount of graduated contributions paid by the deceased;
-- src:172 | (b) determining that weekly rate as if any provisions in orders under section 150 of the Administration Act (annual up-rating of benefits) which—
-- src:173 | (i) increase that weekly rate; and
-- src:174 | (ii) have come into force since the date of the deceased’s death,
-- src:175 | had come into force before that date; and
-- src:176 | (c) excluding any addition under—
-- src:177 | (i) section 36(4) of the 1965 Act; or
-- src:178 | (ii) section 37(1) of that Act.
@ref Regulation 16(4) and (5) (src:169-178)
GIVEN spouse IS A InheritedAmountFacts
GIVETH A NUMBER
`regulation 16(4): the inherited amount, in pounds per week` spouse MEANS
    spouse's `the weekly rate of the deceased's graduated retirement benefit, determined in accordance with regulation 16(5)` DIVIDED BY 2

§§ `Regulation 15: the survivor's state pension based on inheritance of graduated retirement benefit`

DECLARE MarriageFacts HAS
    `the date the marriage took place or the civil partnership was formed` IS A DATE

-- Gloss: the person has reached pensionable age; the spouse or civil partner died while
-- they were married or civil partners; the marriage or partnership began before 6 April
-- 2016; and the person is entitled to an inherited amount under regulation 16(1), (2)
-- or (3).
-- src:150 | (2) Such a person is entitled to a state pension if—
-- src:151 | (a) that person has reached pensionable age;
-- src:152 | (b) that person’s spouse died while they were married or that person’s civil partner died while they were civil partners of each other;
-- src:153 | (c) the marriage took place, or the civil partnership was formed, before 6th April 2016; and
-- src:154 | (d) that person is entitled to an inherited amount under regulation 16(1), (2) or (3).
@ref Regulation 15(2) (src:150-154)
GIVEN facts IS A SpouseDeathFacts
      spouse IS A InheritedAmountFacts
      marriage IS A MarriageFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 15(2): the person is entitled to a state pension under regulation 15` facts spouse marriage MEANS
        `the person has reached pensionable age on the day` facts
    AND `the spouse or civil partner died while the two were married or civil partners` facts
    AND marriage's `the date the marriage took place or the civil partnership was formed` LESS THAN `regulation 1(2): the commencement date`
    AND NOT (`regulation 16: which paragraph gives the person an inherited amount` facts spouse EQUALS NOTHING)

-- src:155 | (3) A state pension under this regulation is payable at a weekly rate equal to the inherited amount determined in accordance with regulation 16(4) to (6).
@ref Regulation 15(3) (src:155)
GIVEN facts IS A SpouseDeathFacts
      spouse IS A InheritedAmountFacts
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`regulation 15(3): the weekly rate of the state pension under regulation 15` facts spouse MEANS
    CONSIDER `regulation 16: which paragraph gives the person an inherited amount` facts spouse
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST inheritedCase THEN JUST (`regulation 16(4): the inherited amount, in pounds per week` spouse)

§§ `Regulation 17: up-rating of the survivor's state pension under regulation 15`

-- Gloss. R is the rate of the person's state pension under regulation 15, as paragraph
-- (2) describes it (without any section 7(4) reduction, after any section 14
-- reduction, and without any section 17 increase). S is the sum of the rates of any
-- state pension the person has under section 7 and section 2, 4 or 12 of the 2014 Act.
-- F is the full rate of the state pension. Three situations:
--   S is equal to or higher than F                            -> paragraphs (8), (9)
--   S is below F and R plus S is equal to or less than F      -> paragraphs (3), (4)
--   S is below F and R plus S is more than F                  -> paragraphs (5), (6), (7)
-- (paragraph (3) and paragraph (8) can only both apply when R is nothing and S equals
-- F; then either way the increase is nothing: fork F21.)
-- The answer NOTHING means no paragraph of regulation 17 gives an increase for the event
-- that has happened (for example, an up-rating order when R plus S is no more than F).
-- Percentages are written as numbers: 5% is 5%, or 0.05.
-- src:183 | (1) The rate of a person’s state pension under regulation 15 is to be increased as follows.
-- src:184 | (2) In this regulation, a reference to the rate of a person’s state pension is to the rate—
-- src:185 | (a) without any reduction under Regulations made under section 7(4) (survivor’s pension based on inheritance of additional old state pension) of the 2014 Act (in the case of a state pension under section 7 of the 2014 Act);
-- src:186 | (b) taking into account any reduction under section 14 (pension sharing: reduction in the sharer’s section 4 pension) of the 2014 Act (in the case of a state pension under section 4 of the 2014 Act); and
-- src:187 | (c) without any increase under section 17 of the 2014 Act.
-- src:188 | (3) The rate of the person’s state pension is increased in accordance with paragraph (4) where—
-- src:189 | (a) that rate, when added to the sum of the rate of any state pension to which the person is entitled under section 7 and section 2, 4 or 12 of the 2014 Act (entitlement to state pension at various rates), is equal to or less than the full rate of the state pension; and
-- src:190 | (b) the full rate of the state pension is increased at any time.
-- src:191 | (4) Where paragraph (3) applies—
-- src:192 | (a) the rate of the person’s state pension is increased by the same percentage as the increase in the full rate; and
-- src:193 | (b) that increase of the person’s state pension is to be made at the same time as the increase in the full rate.
-- src:194 | (5) The rate of the person’s state pension is increased in accordance with either or both of paragraphs (6) and (7) where—
-- src:195 | (a) both—
-- src:196 | (i) that rate, when added to the sum of the rate of any state pension to which the person is entitled under section 7 and section 2, 4 or 12 of the 2014 Act, exceeds the full rate of the state pension; and
-- src:197 | (ii) the sum of the rate of any state pension to which the person is entitled under section 7 and section 2, 4 or 12 of the 2014 Act is less than the full rate of the state pension; and
-- src:198 | (b) either or both of the following occurs at any time—
-- src:199 | (i) the full rate of the state pension is increased;
-- src:200 | (ii) an uprating order comes into force.
-- src:201 | (6) Where paragraph (5)(a) and (b)(i) applies, the rate of the person’s state pension is increased—
-- src:202 | (a) by an amount equal to the appropriate percentage of the shortfall immediately before the full rate of the state pension is increased (“the appropriate percentage” means the percentage by which the full rate is increased); and
-- src:203 | (b) at the same time as paragraph (5)(b)(i) applies.
-- src:204 | (7) Where paragraph (5)(a) and (b)(ii) applies, the rate of the person’s state pension is increased—
-- src:205 | (a) by an amount equal to the appropriate percentage of the excess immediately before the uprating order mentioned in paragraph (5)(b)(ii) comes into force (“the appropriate percentage” means the percentage specified in that uprating order); and
-- src:206 | (b) at the same time as that uprating order comes into force.
-- src:207 | (8) The rate of the person’s state pension is increased in accordance with paragraph (9) where—
-- src:208 | (a) the sum of the rate of any state pension to which the person is entitled under section 7 and section 2, 4 or 12 of the 2014 Act is equal to or higher than the full rate of the state pension; and
-- src:209 | (b) an uprating order comes into force at any time.
-- src:210 | (9) Where paragraph (8) applies—
-- src:211 | (a) the rate of the person’s state pension is increased by the percentage specified in the uprating order mentioned in paragraph (8)(b); and
-- src:212 | (b) that increase of the person’s state pension is to be made at the same time as that uprating order comes into force.
-- src:213 | (10) In this regulation—
-- src:214 | “the excess” means the amount by which the rate of the state pension, when added to the sum of the rate of any state pension to which the person is entitled under section 7 and section 2, 4 or 12 of the 2014 Act, exceeds the full rate;
-- src:215 | “the shortfall” means the amount by which the sum of the rate of any state pension to which the person is entitled under section 7 and section 2, 4 or 12 of the 2014 Act, is less than the full rate;
-- src:216 | “uprating order” means an order under section 151A of the Administration Act (up-rating of transitional state pensions under the 2014 Act).
@ref Regulation 17 (src:183-216)
GIVEN R IS A NUMBER
      S IS A NUMBER
      F IS A NUMBER
      `the percentage by which the full rate is increased, if it is` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the percentage specified in an up-rating order that comes into force, if there is one` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`regulation 17: the increase in the rate of the state pension under regulation 15` R S F `the percentage by which the full rate is increased, if it is` `the percentage specified in an up-rating order that comes into force, if there is one` MEANS
    IF S AT LEAST F
    THEN -- paragraphs (8) and (9)
        CONSIDER `the percentage specified in an up-rating order that comes into force, if there is one`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST orderPercentage THEN JUST (R TIMES orderPercentage)
    ELSE IF R PLUS S AT MOST F
         THEN -- paragraphs (3) and (4)
             CONSIDER `the percentage by which the full rate is increased, if it is`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
             WHEN JUST fullRatePercentage THEN JUST (R TIMES fullRatePercentage)
         ELSE -- paragraphs (5), (6) and (7): the shortfall and the excess
             CONSIDER `the percentage by which the full rate is increased, if it is`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN
                 CONSIDER `the percentage specified in an up-rating order that comes into force, if there is one`
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
                 WHEN JUST orderPercentage THEN JUST (orderPercentage TIMES ((R PLUS S) MINUS F))
             WHEN JUST fullRatePercentage THEN
                 CONSIDER `the percentage specified in an up-rating order that comes into force, if there is one`
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST (fullRatePercentage TIMES (F MINUS S))
                 WHEN JUST orderPercentage THEN JUST ((fullRatePercentage TIMES (F MINUS S)) PLUS (orderPercentage TIMES ((R PLUS S) MINUS F)))

§§ `Regulation 18: choice of lump sum or state pension based on inheritance of deferred graduated retirement benefit`

DECLARE DeferredGrbFacts HAS
    `the spouse's or civil partner's entitlement to graduated retirement benefit was deferred at the time of death` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was deferred throughout the period of 12 months ending with the day before the death` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is entitled to a choice under section 8(2) of the 2014 Act` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Gloss, paragraph (1): (a) the person has reached pensionable age; (b) the spouse or
-- civil partner died while they were married or civil partners; (c) the spouse's GRB was
-- deferred at death and throughout the 12 months ending with the day before; (d) either
-- (i) the person was under pensionable age at the death and did not marry or form a civil
-- partnership before reaching it, or (ii) was over pensionable age at the death.
-- src:218 | (1) Subject to paragraph (8), a person is entitled to a choice under this regulation if—
-- src:219 | (a) that person has reached pensionable age;
-- src:220 | (b) that person’s spouse died while they were married or that person’s civil partner died while they were civil partners of each other;
-- src:221 | (c) the spouse’s or civil partner’s entitlement to graduated retirement benefit was deferred at the time of death and throughout the period of 12 months ending with the day before the death; and
-- src:222 | (d) either—
-- src:223 | (i) that person was under pensionable age when the spouse or civil partner died and did not marry or form a civil partnership between the date of death and the date that person reached pensionable age; or
-- src:224 | (ii) that person was over pensionable age when the spouse or civil partner died.
@ref Regulation 18(1) paragraphs (a) to (d) (src:218-224)
GIVEN facts IS A SpouseDeathFacts
      deferred IS A DeferredGrbFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 18(1): the conditions for a choice are met` facts deferred MEANS
        `the person has reached pensionable age on the day` facts
    AND `the spouse or civil partner died while the two were married or civil partners` facts
    AND deferred's `the spouse's or civil partner's entitlement to graduated retirement benefit was deferred at the time of death`
    AND deferred's `it was deferred throughout the period of 12 months ending with the day before the death`
    AND (   (       `the person's age when the spouse or civil partner died` facts EQUALS `under pensionable age`
                AND NOT (facts's `the person has married or formed a civil partnership between the date of death and the date they reached pensionable age`))
         OR `the person's age when the spouse or civil partner died` facts EQUALS `over pensionable age`)

-- Gloss, paragraph (8): a person who has a choice under section 8(2) of the 2014 Act
-- does not get a second choice under this regulation.
@ref Regulation 18(1) and (8) (src:218-224) (src:240)
GIVEN facts IS A SpouseDeathFacts
      deferred IS A DeferredGrbFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 18(1) and (8): the person is entitled to a choice under regulation 18` facts deferred MEANS
        `regulation 18(1): the conditions for a choice are met` facts deferred
    AND NOT (deferred's `the person is entitled to a choice under section 8(2) of the 2014 Act`)

-- Paragraphs (9), (10) and (11) treat the person who meets paragraph (1) but has a
-- section 8(2) choice: their section 8(2) choice decides what they are paid.
-- src:240 | (8) A person is not entitled to a choice under this regulation if they are entitled to a choice under section 8(2) of the 2014 Act.
@ref Regulation 18(8) (src:240)
GIVEN facts IS A SpouseDeathFacts
      deferred IS A DeferredGrbFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 18(8): paragraph (1) applies but the person has a section 8(2) choice instead` facts deferred MEANS
        `regulation 18(1): the conditions for a choice are met` facts deferred
    AND deferred's `the person is entitled to a choice under section 8(2) of the 2014 Act`

-- Gloss, the date the person becomes entitled to make the choice: the day the last of the
-- conditions in paragraph (1) is met. For a person under pensionable age at the death it
-- is the day they reach pensionable age; for a person over it, the day of the death. That
-- is the later of the two dates (fork F22: derived from paragraph (1), not stated).
@ref Regulation 18(1) (src:218-224)
GIVEN facts IS A SpouseDeathFacts
GIVETH A DATE
`regulation 18(1): the date on which the person becomes entitled to make the choice` facts MEANS
    IF facts's `the date the person reaches pensionable age` GREATER THAN facts's `the date the spouse or civil partner died`
    THEN facts's `the date the person reaches pensionable age`
    ELSE facts's `the date the spouse or civil partner died`

-- Paragraph (4): the period for the choice is the period in regulation 4(2) and (3).
-- Regulation 4(1) is for a person within section 8(1), so it is not used; the period
-- functions of regulation 4(2) and (3) are. The field "falls within section 8(1)" is not
-- read by regulation 4(3) and is a fixed placeholder here.
-- src:229 | (4) The period within which that choice is to be made is the period set out in regulation 4(2) and (3) and a person may make a late choice after that period where—
@ref Regulation 18(4) (src:229)
GIVEN `the date in the most recent notice, issued before the choice was made, confirming that the person may make the choice, if any` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the person claims a state pension` IS A DATE
      facts IS A SpouseDeathFacts
      `the date the person makes the choice` IS A DATE
GIVETH A ChoiceTiming
`regulation 18(4): whether the choice is made within the period` `the date in the most recent notice, issued before the choice was made, confirming that the person may make the choice, if any` `the date the person claims a state pension` facts `the date the person makes the choice` MEANS
    IF `the date the person makes the choice` AT LEAST period's `the first day of the period for the choice`
       AND `the date the person makes the choice` AT MOST period's `the last day of the period for the choice`
    THEN `the choice is within the period`
    ELSE `the choice is outside the period`
    WHERE
        period MEANS
            CONSIDER `the date in the most recent notice, issued before the choice was made, confirming that the person may make the choice, if any`
            WHEN JUST noticeDate THEN `regulation 4(2): the period for the choice where a notice has been issued` noticeDate
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `regulation 4(3): the period for the choice where the person chooses before any notice` periodFacts
        periodFacts MEANS
            ChoicePeriodFacts WITH
                `the person falls within section 8(1) of the 2014 Act` IS FALSE
                `the date in the most recent notice, issued before the choice was made, confirming that the person may make the choice, if any` IS NOTHING
                `the date the person claims a state pension` IS `the date the person claims a state pension`
                `the date the person's spouse or civil partner died` IS facts's `the date the spouse or civil partner died`
                `the date the person makes the choice` IS `the date the person makes the choice`

-- Paragraphs (4)(a) and (b): a late choice, on the same conditions as regulation 4(4)
-- with "a lump sum under regulation 19" in place of "under section 8(4)".
-- src:229 | (4) The period within which that choice is to be made is the period set out in regulation 4(2) and (3) and a person may make a late choice after that period where—
-- src:230 | (a) the Secretary of State considers it is reasonable in any particular case; and
-- src:231 | (b) any amount paid by way of (or on account of) a lump sum under regulation 19 has been repaid to the Secretary of State—
-- src:232 | (i) in full; and
-- src:233 | (ii) in the currency in which that amount was originally paid.
@ref Regulation 18(4) (src:229-233)
GIVEN facts IS A LateChoiceFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 18(4): a late choice may be made` facts MEANS
    `regulation 4(4): a late choice may be made` facts

-- Paragraph (6): a late choice for a state pension reduces the lump sum under regulation 19
-- to nil; regulation 4(5) does the same for section 8.
-- src:235 | (6) The amount of any lump sum to be paid to the person under regulation 19 is reduced to nil where the person makes a late choice under paragraph (4) to be paid a state pension under regulation 20.
@ref Regulation 18(6) (src:235)
GIVEN `the amount of the lump sum that would otherwise be paid under regulation 19` IS A NUMBER
      `the person makes a late choice under regulation 18(4) to be paid a state pension under regulation 20` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`regulation 18(6): the amount of the lump sum` `the amount of the lump sum that would otherwise be paid under regulation 19` `the person makes a late choice under regulation 18(4) to be paid a state pension under regulation 20` MEANS
    `regulation 4(5): the amount of the lump sum` `the amount of the lump sum that would otherwise be paid under regulation 19` `the person makes a late choice under regulation 18(4) to be paid a state pension under regulation 20`

-- Paragraph (7): the choice may be altered as regulation 6(2) says, reading section 8 as
-- regulation 19 and section 9 as regulation 20: the facts in AlterationFacts that name
-- section 8 or 9 are read in that way.
-- src:236 | (7) A choice under this regulation may be altered in the circumstances specified in regulation 6(2), and for that purpose—
-- src:237 | (a) regulation 6(3) applies where the circumstance in regulation 6(2)(f) applies;
-- src:238 | (b) any references in regulation 6(2) and (3) to section 8 of the 2014 Act are to be read as references to regulation 19; and
-- src:239 | (c) any references in regulation 6(2) and (3) to section 9 of the 2014 Act are to be read as references to regulation 20.
@ref Regulation 18(7) (src:236-239)
GIVEN facts IS A AlterationFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 18(7): the choice may be altered` facts MEANS
    `regulation 6(1): the choice may be altered` facts

DECLARE PaymentOutcome IS ONE OF
    `a lump sum under regulation 19`
    `a state pension under regulation 20`
    `regulation 18 does not cover the person`

DECLARE GrbChoiceOutcomeFacts HAS
    `paragraph (1) applies to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the choice the person made, if any` IS A MAYBE PaymentChoice
    `the choice was made in the manner required and within the period, or is a late choice that may be made` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the choice the person asks to change to, if any` IS A MAYBE PaymentChoice
    `the choice may be altered under regulation 6` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Gloss: what the person is to be paid. A person who made no valid choice in time gets a
-- lump sum (5) and (11). A choice (made under regulation 18 or, for a person with a
-- section 8(2) choice, under section 8(2)) of a lump sum gives the lump sum under
-- regulation 19 and of a state pension gives the state pension under regulation 20, (2),
-- (9). An alteration allowed by regulation 6(2) puts the new choice in its place, (7)
-- and (10).
-- A choice not made in the manner (3) requires is treated as no choice (fork F19).
-- src:225 | (2) The person may choose to be paid—
-- src:226 | (a) a lump sum under regulation 19; or
-- src:227 | (b) a state pension under regulation 20.
@ref Regulation 18(2), (5), (9), (10) and (11) (src:225-227)
GIVEN facts IS A GrbChoiceOutcomeFacts
GIVETH A PaymentOutcome
`regulation 18: what the person is to be paid` facts MEANS
    IF NOT (facts's `paragraph (1) applies to the person`)
    THEN `regulation 18 does not cover the person`
    ELSE CONSIDER choiceInForce
         WHEN JUST `a state pension` THEN `a state pension under regulation 20`
         WHEN JUST `a lump sum` THEN `a lump sum under regulation 19`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN `a lump sum under regulation 19`
    WHERE
        originalChoice MEANS
            IF facts's `the choice was made in the manner required and within the period, or is a late choice that may be made`
            THEN facts's `the choice the person made, if any`
            ELSE NOTHING
        choiceInForce MEANS
            IF facts's `the choice may be altered under regulation 6`
            THEN facts's `the choice the person asks to change to, if any`
            ELSE originalChoice

§§ `Regulation 19: the survivor's lump sum`

-- Gloss: the lump sum is the amount calculated under paragraph 10 or 20 of Schedule 1 to
-- the Social Security (Graduated Retirement Benefit) Regulations 2005 (not an input, so
-- the amount is an input). Under paragraph (2), the date those paragraphs call the date
-- the person becomes entitled to a Category A or B pension or to graduated retirement
-- benefit is read as the date the person becomes entitled to make a choice under
-- regulation 18.
-- src:249 | (1) Where a person is to be paid a lump sum by virtue of regulation 18, they are entitled to a lump sum calculated in accordance with paragraph 10 or, where appropriate, paragraph 20 of Schedule 1 to the Social Security (Graduated Retirement Benefit) Regulations 2005.
@ref Regulation 19(1) (src:249)
GIVEN outcome IS A PaymentOutcome
      `the lump sum calculated under paragraph 10 or 20 of Schedule 1 to the 2005 Regulations` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`regulation 19(1): the lump sum payable` outcome `the lump sum calculated under paragraph 10 or 20 of Schedule 1 to the 2005 Regulations` MEANS
    CONSIDER outcome
    WHEN `a lump sum under regulation 19` THEN JUST `the lump sum calculated under paragraph 10 or 20 of Schedule 1 to the 2005 Regulations`
    WHEN `a state pension under regulation 20` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `regulation 18 does not cover the person` THEN NOTHING

-- src:250 | (2) In paragraphs 10(6) and 20(6) of Schedule 1 to those Regulations as they apply for the purposes of this regulation, the references to the date on which the person becomes entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension or to graduated retirement benefit are to be read as a reference to the date on which the person becomes entitled to make a choice under regulation 18.
@ref Regulation 19(2) (src:250)
GIVEN facts IS A SpouseDeathFacts
GIVETH A DATE
`regulation 19(2): the date read in place of the date of becoming entitled to a retirement pension or graduated retirement benefit` facts MEANS
    `regulation 18(1): the date on which the person becomes entitled to make the choice` facts

§§ `Regulation 20: the survivor's state pension based on inheritance of deferred graduated retirement benefit`

DECLARE IncreaseFacts HAS
    `the spouse or civil partner was entitled to an increase in graduated retirement benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the spouse's or civil partner's entitlement to graduated retirement benefit was deferred when they died` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Gloss: paragraph (1)(a) to (d) all must be met; and (e) for a person who has a choice
-- under regulation 18, that they have chosen a state pension; (f) for a person with a
-- section 8(2) choice, that they are to be paid a state pension by regulation 18(9)(b) or
-- (10)(b). For anyone else, neither (e) nor (f) bites. Both come to this: the answer of
-- regulation 18 (what the person is to be paid) is not a lump sum.
-- src:252 | (1) A person is entitled to a state pension under this regulation if—
-- src:253 | (a) that person has reached pensionable age;
-- src:254 | (b) that person’s spouse died while they were married or that person’s civil partner died while they were civil partners of each other;
-- src:255 | (c) either—
-- src:256 | (i) that person was under pensionable age when the spouse or civil partner died and did not marry or form a civil partnership between the date of death and the date that person reached pensionable age; or
-- src:257 | (ii) that person was over pensionable age when the spouse or civil partner died;
-- src:258 | (d) either—
-- src:259 | (i) that person’s spouse or civil partner was entitled to an increase in graduated retirement benefit; or
-- src:260 | (ii) that person’s spouse’s or civil partner’s entitlement to graduated retirement benefit was deferred when the spouse or civil partner died;
-- src:261 | (e) in the case of a person entitled to a choice under regulation 18, that person has chosen to be paid a state pension under this regulation; and
-- src:262 | (f) in the case of a person who is not entitled to a choice under regulation 18 because regulation 18(8) applies to them, that person is to be paid a state pension under this regulation by virtue of regulation 18(9)(b) or (10)(b).
@ref Regulation 20(1) (src:252-262)
GIVEN facts IS A SpouseDeathFacts
      increase IS A IncreaseFacts
      outcome IS A PaymentOutcome
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 20(1): the person is entitled to a state pension under regulation 20` facts increase outcome MEANS
        `the person has reached pensionable age on the day` facts
    AND `the spouse or civil partner died while the two were married or civil partners` facts
    AND (   (       `the person's age when the spouse or civil partner died` facts EQUALS `under pensionable age`
                AND NOT (facts's `the person has married or formed a civil partnership between the date of death and the date they reached pensionable age`))
         OR `the person's age when the spouse or civil partner died` facts EQUALS `over pensionable age`)
    AND (   increase's `the spouse or civil partner was entitled to an increase in graduated retirement benefit`
         OR increase's `the spouse's or civil partner's entitlement to graduated retirement benefit was deferred when they died`)
    AND (   outcome EQUALS `a state pension under regulation 20`
         OR outcome EQUALS `regulation 18 does not cover the person`)

-- Gloss, paragraph (2): the weekly rate is half the weekly rate of the deceased's increase
-- in graduated retirement benefit (an increase under section 36(4) of the 1965 Act,
-- paragraph (5)); where the spouse's benefit was deferred, the increase that would have
-- been payable had the deferral ended just before the death, determined as paragraph (4)
-- says. That determination needs the section 150 orders and the 1965 Act (not inputs):
-- its result is the input.
-- src:263 | (2) Subject to paragraph (3), a state pension under this regulation is payable at a weekly rate equal to half of the weekly rate of—
-- src:264 | (a) the deceased spouse’s or civil partner’s increase in graduated retirement benefit; or
-- src:265 | (b) where the deceased spouse’s or civil partner’s entitlement to graduated retirement benefit was deferred when they died, the increase in graduated retirement benefit, determined in accordance with paragraph (4), that would have been payable if the deferral had ended immediately before their death.
@ref Regulation 20(2) (src:263-265)
GIVEN `the weekly rate of the deceased's increase in graduated retirement benefit, determined as regulation 20(4) requires` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`regulation 20(2): the weekly rate of the state pension under regulation 20` `the weekly rate of the deceased's increase in graduated retirement benefit, determined as regulation 20(4) requires` MEANS
    `the weekly rate of the deceased's increase in graduated retirement benefit, determined as regulation 20(4) requires` DIVIDED BY 2

-- Gloss, paragraph (3): when an order under section 151A of the Administration Act comes
-- into force, the person's rate goes up by the percentage the order specifies.
-- src:266 | (3) For the purposes of paragraph (2), if at any time an order under section 151A of the Administration Act comes into force, the rate of the person’s state pension under this regulation is increased (at that time) by the percentage specified in the order.
@ref Regulation 20(3) (src:266)
GIVEN `the rate of the person's state pension under regulation 20` IS A NUMBER
      `the percentage specified in the order` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`regulation 20(3): the rate after an order under section 151A of the Administration Act` `the rate of the person's state pension under regulation 20` `the percentage specified in the order` MEANS
    `the rate of the person's state pension under regulation 20` TIMES (1 PLUS `the percentage specified in the order`)
